description:
## BLUF

KS-1333 made the four `anchorStateSync` writers persist an unknown block number as `null` instead of a fabricated `0`. Five other places still write a height of 0 for a document whose height is not known, so a document can carry `null` (after a sync) or `0` (at creation, or after a failed anchor) for the same fact.

## Recommendation

Decide once whether the stored blob uses `null` for "not known". KS-1333's direction was yes: the blob type already allows `number | null`, and every reader in this repo handles null (the gateway's persisted guard needs an integer > 0 and refuses 0 and null alike; originate's heal ends in `?? 0`; the frontends fall back with `||`). If yes, change these five with one cell each.

## Detail (read at develop `361537eed238`, 2026-10-12)

* `services/originate/src/routes/documents.ts:883` `blockHeight: 0` (the placeholder blob written when an anchor is requested);
* `:905` `blockHeight: anchorData.blockHeight || 0`;
* `:938` `blockHeight: 0`;
* `:1386` `blockHeight: ad.blockHeight || 0`;
* `services/originate/src/services/anchorStateSync.ts:191` `blockHeight: prior?.blockHeight ?? 0` (the failed-anchor writer: with a null prior it writes 0 back, undoing KS-1333 on that path).
* `services/originate/src/routes/verification.ts:368` (becomes :346 once #1500 merges, because it removes the moved `toBlockHeight` above it) and `services/originate/src/routes/verificationV2.ts:148` `blockHeight: toBlockHeight(chain.blockNumber) ?? blob.blockHeight ?? 0`: the two heal paths that persist through `persistHealedAnchor` end in `?? 0`, so they can turn the NULL that KS-1333 now stores back into 0 (found by the Sonnet gate on #1500, finding Minor).

## Not claimed

That any reader breaks today: none does (see above). The cost is inconsistency, a stored 0 that reads as a claim. Nothing deploys because of this. Raised while doing KS-1333 item 4; the decision and the measurement are on KS-1333.
